-- title:
--   Transport of a cyclotomic level automorphism to the k₀-chart
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime, $M'$ is a non-zero natural number with $q \nmid M'$, and $\ell_g$ is a prime with $\ell_g \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ which divides $M'$ and is assumed to lie in `M'.primeFactors`.
--
--   **The reduction frame over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$.** $A$ is a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` with `A.LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. $q$ lies in the non-units of $A$. $W$ is a finite set of places of the field `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` (the subfield of $\operatorname{ResidueField} A$-Laurent series generated by `jqModC` and its $M'$-fold $q$-expansion) over $\operatorname{ResidueField} A$, and the hypothesis `hW` says that $W$ consists exactly of the members of `ssPlaces q M' (ResidueField A)`: the places $w$ which are rational (the structure map of the residue field of $w$ is surjective), satisfy the predicate `IsAffineGeomPlace`, and whose value `w.evalAt (jGeomGen …)` lies in `ssJSet q (ResidueField A)`, the set of elements $j$ such that every elliptic Weierstrass curve with $j$-invariant $j$ has no non-zero $q$-torsion point. The hypothesis `hle` asserts the inclusion `modularFunctionFieldBar M' ≤ fieldBar q M'` of the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-base change of the full level-$M'$ modular function field into the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-function field of $X_H$ of level $q^2M'$, $H$ being the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb Z/q)^\times$. $R_0$ is a `ConstantReduction` datum for $A$ from `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` to `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'`: a valuation subring `R₀.integers` of the source whose intersection with the constants is $A$, a surjective residue homomorphism onto the target whose kernel is the maximal ideal and which on constants is the residue map of $A$, together with a degree-preserving map on places compatible with orders of functions, and a scaling clause producing non-zero residues. The hypothesis `hR₀` says that for a Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose coefficientwise image in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-Laurent series lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, that element lies in `R₀.integers` and its $R_0$-residue is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$ modulo the maximal ideal of $A$.
--
--   **The small constants $k_0$.** $k_0$ is an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ and $\pi_0 \in k_0$ an element lying in $A$; write $A_0 =$ `A.comap (algebraMap k₀ (AlgebraicClosure ℚ))` for the contraction of $A$ to $k_0$. The hypotheses on $A_0$ are: `hdvr`, $A_0$ is a discrete valuation ring; `hunif`, its maximal ideal is generated by $\pi_0$; `hhens`, $A_0$ is a henselian local ring; `hres`, the residue field of $A_0$ is algebraically closed; and `hκ`, every element of $A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to an element of $k_0$ lying in $A$.
--
--   **The level datum.** $\xi \in k_0$ is a primitive $q$-th root of unity, and `hιξ` provides a ring homomorphism $k_0 \to \mathbb C$ sending $\xi$ to $\exp(2\pi i/q)$. $H_1$ is a subgroup of $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times$, and `hH₁` identifies it as the intersection of `levelH q M'`, the kernel of $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb Z/q)^\times$, with the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb Z/\ell_g)^\times$; thus $H_1$ consists of the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$ and modulo $\ell_g$. $K$ is an intermediate field of $\operatorname{LaurentSeries}(k_0)/k_0$, equal by `hK` to the $k_0$-base change `laurentBaseChange k₀ (xHFunctionField (q ^ 2 * M') H₁)` of the rational function field of $X_{H_1}$ of level $q^2M'$; $K$ is an $A_0$-algebra compatibly with $k_0$, and $j \in K$ is the element whose Laurent series is `coeffEmb k₀ jq`, assumed non-zero. Write $C' =$ `TwoChartIntegralModel.chartAlgFin A₀ K j`, the $A_0$-subalgebra of elements of $K$ integral over $A_0[j]$. The hypotheses `hjK` and `hjC` say that `coeffEmb k₀ jq` lies in $K$ and that the resulting element of $K$ lies in $C'$.
--
--   **Moduli-theoretic package over $A_0$.** Four functoriality hypotheses and three structures are assumed, all over arbitrary commutative $A_0$-algebras $T$: `hℓ`, the $\Gamma_1(\ell_g)$-point condition `IsGamma1Point` (the affine Weierstrass equation at $(x_P,y_P)$, the vanishing of `preΨ ℓg` at $x_P$, and $x_Q = x_P$, $y_Q = y_P$) is carried by a variable change $C$ to the corresponding condition for $C \bullet W$ and `D.variableChange C`; `hM`, the condition `IsGamma0PowAt W p k h` (`IsTwoKernel h` when $p^k = 2$, and `IsCyclicGenKernel p k h` otherwise) is carried by $C$ to `IsGamma0PowAt (C • W) p k (kernelVariableChangeDeg C (gamma0PowDeg p k) h)`; $\mathcal G$ is a family `GroupLaws A₀` of relative group laws on the Proj models of projective Weierstrass curves with unit discriminant, assumed chord-tangent (`h𝒢`: existence of a points-evaluation equivalence additive for the group law and equivariant for Galois twists) and origin-normalised (`h𝒢O`: existence of a ring homomorphism from the origin chart ring presenting the identity section and killing $x/y$ and $z/y$); $\mathcal T$ is a `LevelTransport A₀ 𝒢 q`, a transport of raw Drinfeld pairs along $A_0$-algebra maps and variable changes preserving the Drinfeld-basis condition, assumed to be a section transport (`h𝒯`: the transported sections agree with the original ones after composition with the Proj-level variable-change, respectively coefficient, morphisms); `hVC` and `hCO` provide, for every projective Weierstrass curve over $T$, graded ring homomorphisms of its Proj coordinate ring realising a given variable change, respectively a given $A_0$-algebra map on coefficients, subject to the stated inclusion of irrelevant ideals and to `IsVariableChangeHom`, respectively `IsCoefficientHom`.
--
--   **The cyclotomic chart.** $L_1$ is a field of characteristic zero which is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb Q$ for $\{q\ell_g\}$, with $\zeta_1 \in L_1$ a primitive $q$-th root of unity, $\xi_1 \in L_1$ a primitive $q\ell_g$-th root of unity and $\zeta_1 = \xi_1^{\ell_g}$. $K_1$ is the intermediate field of $\operatorname{LaurentSeries}(L_1)/L_1$ equal to `laurentBaseChange L₁ (xHFunctionField (q ^ 2 * M') H₁)`. $A_1$ is a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L_1$ such that $q$ lies in its maximal ideal and $\zeta_1$ lies in its image in $L_1$; $K_1$ is an $A_1$-algebra compatibly with $L_1$; $j_1 \in K_1$ has Laurent series `coeffEmb L₁ jq` and is assumed non-zero; $\varpi_1$ generates the maximal ideal of $A_1$. Write $C_1 =$ `TwoChartIntegralModel.chartAlgFin A₁ K₁ j₁`. Further, $z_1$ is a point of the scheme `TwoChartIntegralModel A₁ K₁ j₁` (the pushout of the two chart spectra), $\varpi_{z_1}$ is the germ at $z_1$ of the global function obtained from $\varpi_1$ through the structure morphism `TwoChartIntegralModel.toBase` to $\operatorname{Spec} A_1$ (this is the content of `hϖz₁`), and `hz₁` requires $\varpi_{z_1}$ to lie in the maximal ideal of the stalk at $z_1$. The point $y_1$ of $\operatorname{Spec} C_1$ satisfies `hy₁`: its image under `ιFin` is $z_1$. The hypothesis `hss₁` expresses that $y_1$ is supersingular: for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi : C_1 \to \Omega$ with kernel $y_1$, the image $\varphi(\mathtt{jChartFin})$ lies in `ssJSet q Ω`.
--
--   **The comparison of constants.** $\iota : L_1 \to k_0$ is a ring homomorphism with $\iota(\zeta_1) = \xi$, such that $\iota$ carries $A_1$ into $A$ (`hιA`) and such that any $x \in L_1$ with $\iota(x) \in A$ already comes from $A_1$ (`hιA'`).
--
--   **Conclusion.** Let $\gamma \in \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z)$ lie in $\Gamma_0(M')$ and satisfy $\gamma_{11} \equiv 1 \pmod{\ell_g}$, let $\tau_1$ be an $L_1$-algebra automorphism of $K_1$ which is a level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$ in the sense of `IsLevelAutAt L₁ q ζ₁ q (q ^ 2 * M') H₁ γ⁻¹ K₁ τ₁` — that is, for all weights $k$, all modular forms $f, g$ for $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$ of weight $k$ with integral $q$-expansions $p_f, p_g$, $p_g$ having non-zero image in $\operatorname{LaurentSeries}(\mathbb Q)$, all $x \in K_1$ whose Laurent series is the image of $p_f/p_g$, and every embedding $L_1 \to \mathbb C$ sending $\zeta_1$ to $\exp(2\pi i/q)$, the image of $\tau_1 x$ under that embedding times the $q$-expansion of $g \mid_k \mathtt{conjElemN } q\, \gamma^{-1}$ equals the $q$-expansion of $f \mid_k \mathtt{conjElemN } q\, \gamma^{-1}$, the matrix $\mathtt{conjElemN } q\, \delta$ being $\begin{pmatrix} \delta_{00} & \delta_{01}/q \\ q\,\delta_{10} & \delta_{11}\end{pmatrix}$ — and let `hpres₁` be a proof that $\tau_1$ maps $C_1$ into itself. Then there exist a ring homomorphism $c : C_1 \to C'$, a $k_0$-algebra automorphism $\tau$ of $K$, a proof that $\tau$ is a level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$ in the sense of `IsLevelAutAt k₀ q ξ q (q ^ 2 * M') H₁ γ⁻¹ K τ`, a proof `hpres` that $\tau$ maps $C'$ into itself, an element $s$ of $W$, and a maximal ideal $y'$ of $C'$ containing the image of $\pi_0$ under `algebraMap A₀ C'`, such that the following four assertions hold.
--
--   (i) For every $a \in C_1$, the Laurent series over $k_0$ underlying $c(a)$ is the coefficientwise image under $\iota$ of the Laurent series over $L_1$ underlying $a$; so $c$ is given by `coeffMap ι`.
--
--   (ii) The restriction of $\tau$ to $C'$ composed after $c$ equals $c$ composed after the restriction of $\tau_1$ to $C_1$, i.e. $\tau|_{C'} \circ c = c \circ \tau_1|_{C_1}$ as ring homomorphisms $C_1 \to C'$.
--
--   (iii) `Ideal.comap c y' = y₁.asIdeal`, that is, $c^{-1}(y') = y_1$.
--
--   (iv) The point $y'$ specialises the place $s$ in the following sense. Let $g$ be a Laurent series over $\mathbb Q$ lying in `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` (the field generated over $\mathbb Q$ by the $d$-fold $q$-expansions of `jq` for the divisors $d$ of $M'$), assume that the element of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` determined by `coeffEmb (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) g` lies in `R₀.integers`, assume that for every place $P$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ the inequality $P.\mathrm{ord}(j) \ge 0$ for the element determined by `coeffEmb (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) jq` implies $P.\mathrm{ord}(g) \ge 0$, and assume that the $R_0$-residue of $g$ lies in the valuation subring of the place $s$. Then, for every proof that `coeffEmb k₀ g` lies in $K$ and that the resulting element of $K$ lies in $C'$, and for every element of $k_0$ lying in $A$ whose residue in $\operatorname{ResidueField} A$ equals the value at $s$ of the $R_0$-residue of $g$ (that is, `s.evalAt` of that residue), the difference in $C'$ between the element determined by `coeffEmb k₀ g` and the image of that constant under `algebraMap A₀ C'` lies in $y'$.
--
--   This is the transport step of the $\Gamma_1(\ell_g)$-guarded ("diamond") frame: a level automorphism of the cyclotomic function field $K_1$ over $L_1 = \mathbb Q(\zeta_{q\ell_g})$, together with a supersingular closed point of the $j$-finite chart over the discrete valuation ring $A_1$, is carried coefficientwise along an embedding $\iota : L_1 \to k_0$ of constants to the chart over the admissible small constants $k_0 \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q}$, where the target closed point is exhibited as lying over a supersingular place of the level-$M'$ modular function field in characteristic $q$. It is used by the auxiliary level-one lemmas which evaluate level automorphisms at supersingular points of the two-chart integral model.
